Z||000007||mwbackus||11-28-1999||10:23 AM||||     Like 2fast says, the Fiero Store only offers one for the 4cyl, its part #52510 and costs $359.00, ouch!  <P>     The overbored V6 throttle body that RS Motorsports offers for $177.00 does not seem overly expensive to me.  It could provide a significant performance increase for those with a 3.4 swap, but only very extensively modified 2.8's (ie..3.2 ci) would qualify as good candidates for the larger throttle body.<P><BR>Mike<BR>(Fiero info in my user profile)||||reg||1
Z||000008||superXmotorsports||11-28-1999||10:32 AM||||Sorry about that.  The way it is listed in their catalog is under "Peformance V6"  and it is pictured just above the Holley V6 fuel pump.||||reg||11
Z||000009||theogre||11-28-1999||12:17 PM||||Correct. The Holley unit is for 84-86 only. The entire TBI and manifold are diferant on the DIS motor. They use the 700 TBI which is not interchangable with the older unit at all.||||reg||1
Z||000010||WKDFIRO||11-28-1999||09:00 PM||||Stock intakes for the V6 were the same through 88.  Funny that it wouldn't show 87-88.||||reg||4
Z||000011||Carrolles||11-29-1999||12:39 PM||||The coolant tubes to the throttle body are actually there to supply heat to the throttle body to keep it from icing up.  You get a refrigeration effect when you reduce the pressure in a gas.  This is what happens in a throttle body when the air charge is sucked into the intake.  <P>WKDFIRO - If you start noticing poor performance when it turns wet and cold you might want to hook up the coolant hoses again.||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||11-29-1999||09:54 PM||||Silly me..... V6 not 4....... the 87-88 4's use the 700.||||reg||1
